# answered by claude-opus-5-5, prompt /lib/phil/senses b350a3107fa4, 2026-10-19
morals_influence	one
reason_influence	one
morals_from_reason	one
# "Reason alone" (S1) and "reason of itself" (S3) say the same thing: reason with no help from passion. In both, "influence" means moving us to act or feel.
# A1 needs "derived from reason" to carry morals' power to influence over to "reason alone". Whether it does is a question of the argument's validity, not of a shift in sense, so A1 is not a bridge.
